SH1.0 14-Pin Header Layout (Pinout)

Note: In JST SH connectors, Pin 1 is the pin furthest to the left when you are looking at the connector opening with the metal crimp contacts facing up at you.
The pinout order mapped directly to the 1.0mm 14-pin connector on the board reads as follows:

Pin	Function / GPIO	Description
1	              5V (VBUS / VSYS)	Main 5V power input/output
2	              3.3V	Regulated 3.3V power output
3	              GND	Ground
4	              GPIO 43	UART TX
5	              GPIO 44	UART RX
6	              GPIO 1	General Purpose I/O
7	              GPIO 2	General Purpose I/O
8	              GPIO 41	General Purpose I/O
9	              GPIO 42	General Purpose I/O
10	            GPIO 15	I2C SDA
11	            GPIO 16	I2C SCL
12	            GPIO 3	ADC / Touch Interrupt pin
13	            GND	Ground
14	            GND	Ground


Many of these pins are shared with onboard hardware:
I2C Pins (GPIO 15 & 16) are connected to the internal touch screen controller. Do not pull these high or low externally without keeping protocol conflicts in mind.
UART Pins (GPIO 43 & 44) are hardwired as the default hardware serial port on the ESP32-S3. 
